Subject: [PATCH] Fix OpenCASCADE (OCCT) 8.0.0 build compatibility

OCCT 8.0.0 introduces several source-incompatible changes that break the
IfcOpenShell OpenCASCADE geometry kernel:

  * The per-class legacy `Handle_Xxx` typedefs are no longer generated when a
    class header is included. Replaced all `Handle_Xxx` uses with the
    `Handle(Xxx)` macro (i.e. `opencascade::handle<Xxx>`), which is OCCT's
    recommended migration path.
  * Many headers no longer pull in collection types transitively. Added the
    required explicit includes for the (still shipped, now deprecated)
    `TopTools_*`, `TColgp_*`, `TColStd_*`, `Message_ListOfMsg` and
    `ShapeExtend_DataMapOfShapeListOfMsg` collection aliases.
  * `BRepCheck_ListIteratorOfListOfStatus.hxx` was removed; iterate the status
    list with `NCollection_List<BRepCheck_Status>::Iterator` instead.
  * `Poly_Triangulation::Triangles()` was removed; use `InternalTriangles()`.
  * `NCollection_LinearVector` (BVH arrays) replaced `push_back` with `Append`.
  * `BRepTopAdaptor_FClass2d` became non-copyable/non-movable, so it can no
    longer be stored in a `std::vector` that reserves/relocates; use a
    `std::deque` instead.
  * `NCollection_Array1` construction from `std::size_t` bounds is now
    ambiguous; cast the size to `int` (matching the existing neighbouring code).

This is a downstream patch for the conda-forge occt 8.0.0 migration; upstream
IfcOpenShell had not yet been ported to OCCT 8.0.0 at the time of writing.
Drop this patch once a release containing equivalent fixes is used.
